# Always Open a Pull Request

After every completed development task, commit on a topic branch, push, and open a GitHub pull request. Do not wait for the user to ask.

## Do

- Commit on a short topic branch (no `codex/` prefix).
- Push the branch, then `gh pr create` with a HEREDOC body (Summary + Test plan).
- Return the PR URL when done.
- Parent agent owns commits, issues, and PRs.
- `se-implement` does not commit unless the user already asked.
- Apply this to every development task, including docs/workflow changes.

## Don't

- Do not wait to be asked for a PR.
- Do not leave completed work local-only.
- Do not skip a PR because the change looks small or is "just docs".

## Exception

Tiny typo-only edits may still go directly to `main` when the scope is a single obvious typo. Everything else needs a PR.

Canonical detail: `docs/rules/workflow.md`.
